I implemented a merge logic in `get_openapi_security_definitions` to handle this. When a security scheme of type `oauth2` is encountered and a definition with the same name already exists, the code now iterates through the flows and merges the scopes of each flow. If a flow type is already present, its scopes are updated with the new scopes; otherwise, the new flow is added. For non-OAuth2 schemes, the existing behavior of overwriting is maintained.

